From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:17:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] http.sys: listen where Windows does

- a URL with a "+" or "*" host or a host name listens on all interfaces, an IPv4 address host on that
  address, localhost on the loopback interface only
- the IP listen list (ListenOnlyList) restricts all of them, as on Windows; a URL whose address is not on
  the list gets no socket
- sockets are kept per port and address and shared by URLs; removing the last URL closes its sockets
  (the check for unused sockets counted the entry being removed and never closed them)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

